1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,862
A tightrope walker carries a long pole.

2
00:00:02,862 --> 00:00:05,910
A truck piled high with
hay tips over on a turn.

3
00:00:05,910 --> 00:00:07,999
A toy bird balances on its beak.

4
00:00:08,399 --> 00:00:09,744
Three different scenes.

5
00:00:09,744 --> 00:00:11,667
All three hide one special point.

6
00:00:12,117 --> 00:00:15,696
Aarav cuts a funny shape out of
cardboard for his science model.

7
00:00:15,696 --> 00:00:18,047
He wants to balance it on a pencil tip.

8
00:00:18,397 --> 00:00:19,844
He tries here, and there.

9
00:00:19,844 --> 00:00:20,820
It keeps falling.

10
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,427
So where is the balance point?

11
00:00:22,927 --> 00:00:24,821
A plumb line finds it in two tries.

12
00:00:25,421 --> 00:00:28,177
Every tiny bit of the
cardboard has weight.

13
00:00:28,177 --> 00:00:30,043
Gravity pulls each bit down.

14
00:00:30,393 --> 00:00:33,072
Bits on the left try to
turn the card one way.

15
00:00:33,072 --> 00:00:35,091
Bits on the right, the other way.

16
00:00:35,491 --> 00:00:39,138
There is one point where all
these turning effects cancel out.

17
00:00:39,138 --> 00:00:41,666
That point is the centre of gravity, G.

18
00:00:42,066 --> 00:00:45,672
Put the pencil right under
G, and the card balances.

19
00:00:46,272 --> 00:00:51,171
Now hang the cut-out on a pin, through
a hole called A, and hold it tilted.

20
00:00:51,521 --> 00:00:53,943
Its weight acts at G, straight down.

21
00:00:53,943 --> 00:00:58,042
G is off to one side of the pin,
so the weight turns the card.

22
00:00:58,442 --> 00:01:00,753
It swings past the bottom, and back.

23
00:01:00,753 --> 00:01:02,183
Each swing is smaller.

24
00:01:02,583 --> 00:01:03,546
Slow-mo replay.

25
00:01:03,546 --> 00:01:04,446
Freeze here.

26
00:01:04,770 --> 00:01:08,970
The lever arm is the sideways distance
from the pin to the line of the

27
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:09,870
weight.

28
00:01:09,593 --> 00:01:12,349
Turning effect equals
weight times lever arm.

29
00:01:12,749 --> 00:01:16,484
As G swings under the pin,
the lever arm shrinks to zero.

30
00:01:16,484 --> 00:01:18,647
So the card comes to rest there.

31
00:01:19,247 --> 00:01:23,660
On the graph, the turning effect
swings plus and minus, then dies away

32
00:01:23,660 --> 00:01:24,560
to zero.

33
00:01:24,810 --> 00:01:28,577
Now hang a plumb line from the
same pin, and draw along it.

34
00:01:28,577 --> 00:01:30,719
G must be somewhere on this line.

35
00:01:31,119 --> 00:01:35,188
Next, hang the card from a second
hole, B, and let it settle.

36
00:01:35,588 --> 00:01:36,958
Draw the new line.

37
00:01:36,958 --> 00:01:39,699
The two lines cross at exactly one point.

38
00:01:39,699 --> 00:01:40,971
That point is G.

39
00:01:41,621 --> 00:01:44,392
Is G the same point as the centre of mass?

40
00:01:44,392 --> 00:01:46,177
Let's check, step by step.

41
00:01:46,527 --> 00:01:47,427
Step one.

42
00:01:47,385 --> 00:01:50,848
A bit of mass m sits a
sideways distance x away.

43
00:01:50,848 --> 00:01:54,531
Its weight, m g, turns
the body by m g times x.

44
00:01:55,281 --> 00:01:56,181
Step two.

45
00:01:56,104 --> 00:01:57,449
Add up every bit.

46
00:01:57,449 --> 00:02:00,621
The total turning effect
is the sum of m g x.

47
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:02,271
Step three.

48
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:05,272
If g is the same for every
bit, take it outside.

49
00:02:05,272 --> 00:02:07,884
The total becomes g times the sum of m x.

50
00:02:08,634 --> 00:02:09,534
Step four.

51
00:02:09,466 --> 00:02:13,272
Measured from the centre of
mass, the sum of m x is zero.

52
00:02:13,272 --> 00:02:15,882
So the turning effect is zero there too.

53
00:02:16,632 --> 00:02:20,563
So when g is the same everywhere,
the two points are the same.

54
00:02:21,163 --> 00:02:22,163
Remember this.

55
00:02:22,163 --> 00:02:26,546
The centre of gravity is the point where
the total turning effect of gravity

56
00:02:26,546 --> 00:02:27,446
is zero.

57
00:02:27,966 --> 00:02:30,833
Now the plumb line trick, link by link.

58
00:02:31,183 --> 00:02:33,891
The card hangs still, so
nothing is turning it.

59
00:02:34,291 --> 00:02:38,609
The pin pushes at the pin itself,
so its push has no lever arm.

60
00:02:39,009 --> 00:02:43,015
The weight has no turning effect only
when G is straight below the pin.

61
00:02:43,415 --> 00:02:46,775
So the vertical line through
the pin must pass through G.

62
00:02:46,775 --> 00:02:48,437
Two such lines meet at G.

63
00:02:49,037 --> 00:02:50,127
Side by side.

64
00:02:50,127 --> 00:02:53,670
In a cardboard cut-out, g
is the same at every bit.

65
00:02:53,670 --> 00:02:56,021
So G sits at the centre of mass.

66
00:02:56,421 --> 00:03:00,295
In a very tall tower, g gets
a tiny bit weaker higher up.

67
00:03:00,295 --> 00:03:03,507
So each kilogram at the
top weighs a little less.

68
00:03:04,107 --> 00:03:05,141
Now you try.

69
00:03:05,141 --> 00:03:09,802
In a very tall tower, is the centre
of gravity slightly above or slightly

70
00:03:09,802 --> 00:03:11,610
below the centre of mass?

71
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:12,896
Pause and decide.

72
00:03:16,096 --> 00:03:17,142
Slightly below!

73
00:03:17,142 --> 00:03:19,692
The lower parts are pulled a bit harder.

74
00:03:19,692 --> 00:03:23,250
In everyday objects, the gap
is far too small to notice.

75
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:25,956
G also decides when things tip over.

76
00:03:26,306 --> 00:03:27,231
Tilt a box.

77
00:03:27,231 --> 00:03:31,704
While the line straight down from G
stays inside its base, the weight turns

78
00:03:31,704 --> 00:03:32,604
it back.

79
00:03:32,831 --> 00:03:36,795
Once that line passes the
corner, the weight turns it over.

80
00:03:36,795 --> 00:03:37,695
It tips.

81
00:03:38,166 --> 00:03:39,066
Your turn.

82
00:03:38,969 --> 00:03:42,922
A bus with luggage on its roof,
or the same luggage packed low.

83
00:03:42,922 --> 00:03:44,825
Which tips at a smaller tilt?

84
00:03:44,825 --> 00:03:46,007
Pause and decide.

85
00:03:49,207 --> 00:03:50,402
The roof luggage!

86
00:03:50,402 --> 00:03:54,062
It raises G, so the line from
G passes the wheels sooner.

87
00:03:54,712 --> 00:03:56,402
Now, one worked example.

88
00:03:56,752 --> 00:04:00,649
A box is forty centimetres wide, with
its centre of gravity in the middle,

89
00:04:00,649 --> 00:04:01,852
sixty centimetres up.

90
00:04:01,852 --> 00:04:03,365
At what tilt does it tip?

91
00:04:03,865 --> 00:04:06,768
It tips when the line
from G reaches the corner.

92
00:04:07,518 --> 00:04:10,738
Then tan theta equals half
the width over the height.

93
00:04:10,738 --> 00:04:11,962
Twenty over sixty.

94
00:04:11,962 --> 00:04:13,241
That is one third.

95
00:04:13,991 --> 00:04:16,528
So theta is about eighteen
point four degrees.

96
00:04:17,178 --> 00:04:18,640
Now, the exam trap.

97
00:04:18,990 --> 00:04:22,603
Many students think G must lie
inside the material of the body.

98
00:04:23,003 --> 00:04:23,932
Not always.

99
00:04:23,932 --> 00:04:28,779
For a boomerang, or a bent wire, G
lies in the empty space, outside the

100
00:04:28,779 --> 00:04:29,679
material.

101
00:04:30,196 --> 00:04:31,705
Where is this asked?

102
00:04:31,705 --> 00:04:36,293
In statements on centre of gravity
versus centre of mass, the plumb line

103
00:04:36,293 --> 00:04:37,893
method, and toppling.

104
00:04:38,493 --> 00:04:39,634
Exam level now.

105
00:04:39,634 --> 00:04:44,013
A uniform plate, forty centimetres
by thirty, hangs at rest from a pin

106
00:04:44,013 --> 00:04:45,105
at one corner.

107
00:04:45,105 --> 00:04:49,127
What angle does its forty centimetre
side make with the vertical?

108
00:04:49,127 --> 00:04:50,316
Pause and solve.

109
00:04:55,716 --> 00:04:56,873
The answer is C.

110
00:04:56,873 --> 00:04:58,524
About thirty seven degrees.

111
00:04:59,024 --> 00:05:02,986
At rest, G is straight below the
pin, at the centre of the plate.

112
00:05:03,486 --> 00:05:06,253
So the diagonal from the
pin hangs straight down.

113
00:05:06,753 --> 00:05:10,151
The long side makes an angle
theta with the diagonal.

114
00:05:10,151 --> 00:05:14,694
Tan theta is thirty over forty, so
theta is about thirty seven degrees.

115
00:05:15,294 --> 00:05:16,834
Here is your recap.

116
00:05:16,834 --> 00:05:18,417
Screenshot this card.

117
00:05:21,617 --> 00:05:23,555
Can you answer these without help?

118
00:05:23,955 --> 00:05:24,855
One.

119
00:05:24,367 --> 00:05:28,158
Why must the plumb line from the pin
pass through the centre of gravity?

120
00:05:29,058 --> 00:05:29,958
Two.

121
00:05:29,517 --> 00:05:33,840
When are the centre of gravity and
the centre of mass not the same point?

122
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:35,640
Three.

123
00:05:35,249 --> 00:05:38,266
Why does roof luggage make
a bus tip over more easily?

124
00:05:39,166 --> 00:05:43,397
Next time: spin a ruler about
its middle, then about its end.

125
00:05:43,397 --> 00:05:45,312
Why is one so much harder?

126
00:05:45,312 --> 00:05:46,646
Moment of inertia.
